  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with the four functions that emit `subscription.updated` in their own code. All four are in `billing/subscriptions.py`:\n\n- **`subscriptions.transition`**: it emits `subscription.updated` for every status change except canceling, which emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- **`subscriptions.change_items`**: it emits the event after replacing the items.\n- **`subscriptions.cancel`**: it emits the event when the cancellation is scheduled for period end. An immediate cancel goes through `transition` and emits `subscription.canceled`.\n- **`subscriptions.reactivate`**: it emits the event when it undoes a scheduled cancellation.\n\nCallers of `transition` are excluded, as you asked: `pause`, `resume`, the dunning code and the engine. A search of the `billing` package found no other place that emits this event type, and no other code builds the event type dynamically.\n\nI didn't run the tests, since I only read code and wrote the answer file.",
